OpenABL (https://github.com/OpenHandheldCollective/OpenABL), GPL-3.0-or-later,
(c) Open Handheld Collective. These images are the default-Chinese bilingual
variant of OpenABL 1.1. The complete corresponding source is installed on the
system at /usr/share/doc/OpenABL: the upstream base archive
openabl-v1.1-source.tar.xz plus default-zh.patch, the only source change. Both
files, and the build and provenance notes, are also listed in OpenABL-notices
next to this README.

The images use Simplified Chinese when no language has been stored. Choosing
English in the menu is remembered, and both languages stay selectable.

1. Copy the OpenABL folder from the SD card to the root of Android internal storage.

2. Identify the SoC for your device (flashing the wrong ABL can brick the device,
   so match it carefully):

     SM8250 - AYN Thor Lite
              Retroid Pocket 5, Pocket Flip 2, Pocket Mini, Pocket Mini V2
     SM8550 - AYN Odin 2, Odin 2 Mini, Odin 2 Portal, Thor
              AYANEO Pocket EVO, ACE, DMG, DS, S 1K/2K
              Retroid Pocket 6, Pocket Nova
     SM8650 - AYANEO Pocket S2
              KONKR Pocket FIT (G3 Gen 3)
     SM8750 - AYN Odin 3
              KONKR Pocket FIT (8 Elite)

3. Using "run script as root" in settings, browse to your SoC's folder (e.g.
   OpenABL/SM8750) and run backup_abl.sh to back up your current ABL.

4. Copy the backup (abl_a.img and abl_b.img, written into your SoC folder) to your
   PC for safekeeping.

5. Run flash_abl.sh the same way to flash OpenABL.

6. Reboot holding VOL- to open the OpenABL menu.

7. In the menu (move with VOL-/+, select with POWER):
     - Set Device model
     - Set Boot mode to Linux
     - Choose Start
